--- Render contract classification ---

Per the prompt's enum: RenderNarrative for prose-accumulator
features; RenderProposal for typed draft hand-off features;
RenderSuggestion for single-input prefill features.

Pragmatic policy adopted in this slice:
  - All 54 wireable entries are marked RenderNarrative with empty
    BaselineFormHandoff.
  - Rationale: every shipped component today renders the stream
    output via AIFeatureCard's AiOutputPanel slot as accumulated
    text. No "Apply to form" / "Use this draft" hand-off code paths
    have been implemented yet by predecessor slices — the prompt's
    description of 16 features as Proposal/Suggestion describes
    intended UX, not shipped UX. Marking everything as Narrative
    reflects observable reality and avoids inventing a UX claim
    that the on-mode tests would not back up.
  - The RenderProposal and RenderSuggestion enum values ARE
    defined and the SPAWiringSelfCheck enforces the contract for
    them (non-empty BaselineFormHandoff matching a Registry.Frontend
    path). When a future slice introduces a real "Apply to form"
    hand-off, it flips the RenderContract on its row and the
    self-check enforces the rest.

