=== REASONING ===

W1's job is contract codification + static enforcement, not bulk
component rewrites. The SURVEY data shows the on-the-wire wiring
is already done by predecessor slices F5 (0006) §D6.4 through ML
tier 0064 — 57/57 importable AI components already call useAiStream
and 32 *AIOnWiredCallsRoute*.test.tsx files already exist proving
the call paths fire. What was MISSING was:

  (a) The build-time contract that pairs every feature ID to its
      SPA component and canonical endpoint, so a future slice can
      add a registry entry without a matching component file and
      still get caught at CI time.
  (b) A static check that the placeholder strings (future slice,
      coming soon, wiring lands, would call POST) and the literal-
      disabled-Button antipattern stay out of shipped AI code.
  (c) A static check that every wireable component imports
      useAiStream AND references its endpoint path.
  (d) Methodology entries P11 / P12 making the rules first-class
      principles, not slice-local conventions.

This slice ships exactly those four things. It does NOT modify any
guard.Wrap handler, register any new route, add any new SPA route,
add any new UI test ID, add any new background job, or alter any
client storage key.

ADR-015 invariants this slice touches:

  I3  Baseline intact:        no baseline handler or baseline form
                              touched. SPAWiringTable is a build-
                              time artifact; no runtime path reads
                              it. Verified by grep:
                                PS> grep -r 'SPAWiringTable' web/
                                (no hits — Go-only file)
  I5  Off-mode absence:       no new UI surface introduced.
                              AIChatbotIndicator's comment rewording
                              changes zero pixels. withAiFeature gate
                              behavior unchanged.
  I6  Off-mode 404:           no route added or modified.
  I7  No SQL bypass:          no write path introduced.
  I8  No duplicate writers:   no new mutation hooks introduced.

Methodology principles this slice respects:

  P1  Minimal surface:        Go file count delta = +2 (spa_wiring.go
                              + spa_wiring_test.go). Generated file
                              delta = +1 (web/src/ai/spaWiring.ts).
                              Tool extensions = +2 test files.
  P3  Single source of truth: registry.go remains the canonical
                              feature list. SPAWiringTable cross-
                              references it; SPAWiringSelfCheck
                              fails the build if the two drift.
  P6  AI-Off Contract:        invariants I3/I5/I6/I7/I8/I9/I10
                              unchanged (see AI-OFF CONTRACT
                              section below).
  P9  Typed registry:         the Go-side SPAWiringTable mirrors
                              into web/src/ai/spaWiring.ts via the
                              same tools/aigen pattern that already
                              mirrors features.ts. One source, two
                              consumers.
  P10 Baseline + AI:          ChatbotPage's dual-path
                              (useSendChatMessage baseline +
                              useAiStream AI selected by
                              useAiEnabled) remains the canonical
                              example. W1 does not collapse the
                              two paths.
  P11 NEW — Wired-or-absent:  every entry in SPAWiringTable maps to
                              a Component file that imports
                              useAiStream and references the endpoint
                              (enforced by W1-B + SPAWiringSelfCheck).
  P12 NEW — No placeholder
      buttons:                forbidden substrings + literal
                              disabled={true} / shorthand-disabled
                              on <Button> are rejected by W1-A.

